Update notifications and cancellation implementation

Product behavior:
- Update notifications can be hidden for one exact Beaver, Ollama binary, or Ollama model version; a future version appears again.
- Forecast DEV notifications remain permanent and unchanged.
- Settings now has an Updates page with permanent installed versions, only available Beaver and Ollama binary updates, and manual refresh.
- Active downloads reuse the existing progress, Cancel, and success toast patterns.

Backend decisions:
- Dismissals are validated, bounded to 128 entries, persisted atomically in update-notifications.json, and fail open when the store is invalid.
- Beaver download cancellation targets only the active generation and removes the partial temporary update.
- Ollama cancellation is registered before the release manifest request. A bounded admission wait and late-token cancellation close the immediate-click race while transaction recovery remains authoritative after mutation.
- Ollama model update identity includes the exact remote digest.

UI and assets:
- Beaver reuses the existing splash SVG masks and the established light/dark color-role swap.
- Ollama uses the supplied selfh.st SVGs with CC BY 4.0 attribution in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
- Internal row separators were removed and version values align to the right.
- All user-facing text is translated in the seven supported languages.

Validation:
- Live Ollama update cancelled at 0 percent and returned to the update action in 617 ms; installed version remained 0.32.15 and no partial, temporary, staging, or delete path remained.
- npm test passed, including 480 Vitest files and 2620 tests plus build, CI, CEF, E2E runner, extension-host, and reasoning-fixture checks.
- npm run lint, TypeScript check, cargo fmt check, cargo check, cargo clippy strict, and targeted Rust update, cancellation, cleanup, setup, and persistence tests passed.
- The full Rust suite was not rerun because its deferred-updater helper failure and Terminal PTY failures are documented pre-existing scope.

Commit scope:
- Unrelated Beaver website mockups and fast-mode images were intentionally excluded.
